00:26:46.616 --> 00:26:55.819
Africans are demanding their share of self-determination as a reward for services rendered in millions of deaths and to follow Wilson's principles on the right of peoples to self-determination.

00:26:56.939 --> 00:26:59.780
A diver from the ritual attempts unsuccessfully to gain access to the conference.

00:27:00.180 --> 00:27:00.980
He is Indochinese.

00:27:01.501 --> 00:27:02.441
This is the future Ho Chi Minh.

00:27:07.942 --> 00:27:08.402
At the end of March,

00:27:08.783 --> 00:27:11.243
Wilson eventually presented his League of Nations to the press.

00:27:11.603 --> 00:27:13.964
making it the very heart of the future Treaty of Versailles.

00:27:14.568 --> 00:27:16.590
Clemenceau and Lloyd George are polite,

00:27:17.110 --> 00:27:17.530
Nothing more.

00:27:18.311 --> 00:27:20.793
And the American Congress will never ratify the League of Nations.

00:27:21.274 --> 00:27:22.815
from which Germany will be excluded initially.

00:27:23.655 --> 00:27:25.117
The Treaty of Versailles was stillborn.

00:27:27.078 --> 00:27:35.986
It was a truncated Treaty of Versailles that we had to deal with from the moment America had no presence in the League of Nations institutions.

00:27:37.967 --> 00:27:40.329
In parallel, the International Labour Office was created,

00:27:40.589 --> 00:27:41.550
which still exists

00:27:41.970 --> 00:27:43.752
to secure the emerging working class.

00:27:44.080 --> 00:27:45.700
and fight against unemployment and poverty.

00:27:46.741 --> 00:27:50.202
But the Allies are playing a dangerous game by maintaining a food blockade in Germany.

00:27:50.962 --> 00:27:55.723
This blockade is dividing the Council of

00:28:02.485 --> 00:28:12.028
Four.

00:28:14.040 --> 00:28:16.201
"Not only are we sowing the seeds of hatred for the future,

00:28:16.502 --> 00:28:18.803
We are nurturing a revolution!

00:28:21.725 --> 00:28:23.325
This future hatred that Lloyd George speaks of,

00:28:23.446 --> 00:28:23.946
visionary,

00:28:24.186 --> 00:28:27.268
and the terror of a red revolution that could spread to Germany and the West,

00:28:27.708 --> 00:28:28.729
they are speeding up the discussions.

00:28:29.689 --> 00:28:31.690
The fate of the former German empire must be settled quickly.

00:28:40.756 --> 00:28:41.156
Eventually,

00:28:41.760 --> 00:28:44.303
The conference will settle the peace with Germany in one month.

00:28:44.964 --> 00:28:45.685
Orlando has left.

00:28:46.006 --> 00:28:46.646
and symbolically,

00:28:46.947 --> 00:28:49.610
We leave the Quai d'Orsay for the private mansion of an American banker.

00:28:52.374 --> 00:28:56.078
Each side wants to derive the best provisions for the future of its country from the peace treaty.

00:28:56.839 --> 00:28:58.321
Then the conversations become tense,

00:28:58.722 --> 00:29:00.003
because the interests are so divergent.

00:29:01.676 --> 00:29:02.617
The British,

00:29:03.217 --> 00:29:05.199
they want to maintain,

00:29:05.679 --> 00:29:06.019
obviously,

00:29:06.059 --> 00:29:06.860
their power,

00:29:07.180 --> 00:29:09.081
to maintain their empire,

00:29:09.262 --> 00:29:12.244
this empire on which the sun never sets.

00:29:12.664 --> 00:29:15.206
They are in favor of a firm stance towards Germany.

00:29:15.546 --> 00:29:16.567
And like the French,

00:29:16.627 --> 00:29:17.608
They want reparations.

00:29:17.908 --> 00:29:22.151
They want an extremely large sum in compensation.

00:29:22.671 --> 00:29:23.051
They are even,

00:29:23.292 --> 00:29:23.732
initially,

00:29:23.772 --> 00:29:24.833
more demanding than the French.

00:29:25.013 --> 00:29:26.314
They want the Germans,

00:29:26.374 --> 00:29:27.214
in these repairs,

00:29:28.095 --> 00:29:29.296
reimburse the war portions.

00:29:30.296 --> 00:29:30.876
The French,

00:29:30.997 --> 00:29:31.137
them,

00:29:31.397 --> 00:29:35.099
are obsessed with their borders and have no choice but to take a very hard line.

00:29:36.460 --> 00:29:41.064
Clemenceau will constantly negotiate in order to obtain that

00:29:41.484 --> 00:29:46.307
The British and Americans pledge to ensure the security of France.

00:29:46.487 --> 00:29:48.609
We must not forget that the issue is primarily demographic.

00:29:48.629 --> 00:29:54.613
France has 40 million inhabitants and Germany still has approximately 65 million inhabitants.

00:29:54.713 --> 00:29:56.194
Because of this Franco-German inequality,

00:29:56.195 --> 00:29:58.476
France's security depends on...

00:29:58.776 --> 00:30:00.157
leveling of opportunities,

00:30:00.297 --> 00:30:02.177
Therefore, an extremely harsh treaty is needed.

00:30:02.197 --> 00:30:03.338
Germany must pay.

00:30:03.538 --> 00:30:04.739
Germany needs to be weakened.

00:30:05.019 --> 00:30:10.641
So this absolute conviction that Germany is responsible for the war and that for this it must pay,

00:30:10.701 --> 00:30:14.183
Bosch will pay.

00:30:14.683 --> 00:30:17.764
French and British statesmen knew that they had to make people pay.

00:30:17.764 --> 00:30:18.304
and Germany,

00:30:19.345 --> 00:30:21.847
themselves being ruined.

00:30:23.928 --> 00:30:25.109
And what's even more important,

00:30:25.449 --> 00:30:27.891
The reason is that the people were demanding exemplary peace.

00:30:29.512 --> 00:30:30.773
They wanted a peace between victors,

00:30:31.273 --> 00:30:34.375
where Germany was to be singled out as solely responsible for the war.

00:30:37.357 --> 00:30:38.298
And to a gentle peace,

00:30:38.918 --> 00:30:42.300
Neither Clemenceau nor Lloyd George would have survived politically.

00:30:43.982 --> 00:30:47.364
The French will do everything they can to ensure that the issue...

00:30:48.036 --> 00:30:53.878
The issue of security is at the heart of the debates for one simple reason, ultimately.

00:30:54.358 --> 00:30:57.519
that is, whatever the outcome of the peace treaties,

00:30:58.180 --> 00:31:02.421
France will continue to have a continental border with Germany.

00:31:02.781 --> 00:31:04.402
This is not the case for Great Britain.

00:31:04.403 --> 00:31:05.702
This is not the case in the United States.

00:31:07.903 --> 00:31:08.443
For his part,

00:31:08.843 --> 00:31:10.684
Wilson clings to his idea of ​​a just peace.

00:31:12.860 --> 00:31:22.471
Our biggest mistake would be to give Germany powerful reasons to seek revenge one day.

00:31:22.472 --> 00:31:25.234
They must understand that the occupation of Germany,

00:31:25.454 --> 00:31:27.076
at least for 15 years,

00:31:27.656 --> 00:31:29.899
will prevent them from complying with the treaty.

00:31:30.219 --> 00:31:33.623
I need those 15 years.

00:31:35.516 --> 00:31:36.176
He gets them.

00:31:36.737 --> 00:31:37.217
Later,

00:31:37.657 --> 00:31:42.180
Clemenceau was then able to call French President Poincaré from his office to announce the news.

00:31:48.303 --> 00:31:48.883
Miss,

00:31:49.163 --> 00:31:50.464
the Presidency of the Republic,

00:31:50.484 --> 00:31:50.984
Please.

00:31:53.466 --> 00:31:54.186
Mr. President,

00:31:55.026 --> 00:31:55.727
I am 15 years old.

00:31:56.467 --> 00:31:57.248
Peace has been made.

00:32:05.148 --> 00:32:06.610
The clauses of the treaty are being refined.

00:32:07.031 --> 00:32:10.675
We will destroy part of the weaponry and reduce the German army to 100,000 men.

00:32:11.196 --> 00:32:11.637
NOW,

00:32:11.917 --> 00:32:12.678
We need to act quickly.

00:32:12.998 --> 00:32:13.359
Early May,

00:32:13.759 --> 00:32:16.022
The Germans are summoned to the Trianon hotel in Versailles.

00:32:19.487 --> 00:32:19.927
Gentlemen!

00:32:20.916 --> 00:32:23.778
This is neither the time nor the place for superfluous talk.

00:32:24.359 --> 00:32:34.987
Before you are representatives of the nations that united to resist a war that was imposed upon us for more than four years in a most cruel manner.

00:32:36.552 --> 00:32:37.212
Do you want peace?

00:32:37.753 --> 00:32:39.454
We are willing to grant it to you.

00:32:39.734 --> 00:32:42.216
Here is the book containing our provisions.

00:32:42.696 --> 00:32:43.577
The Treaty of Versailles,

00:32:43.597 --> 00:32:44.738
That's 400 clauses.

00:32:44.918 --> 00:32:47.159
These 400 clauses are very harsh for Germany.

00:32:47.259 --> 00:32:51.182
She acknowledges that Germany will lose part of its territory.

00:32:51.242 --> 00:32:54.064
Germany will have to pay war reparations.

00:32:54.104 --> 00:32:55.926
because she is the one responsible for the war.

00:32:56.386 --> 00:32:56.946
But all of that,

00:32:57.026 --> 00:32:59.768
It happened in a particular context.

00:33:00.729 --> 00:33:02.990
We know the identity of the hater,

00:33:03.090 --> 00:33:03.991
because we are there.

00:33:11.836 --> 00:33:18.119
We know the intensity of the hatred we are facing.

00:33:18.120 --> 00:33:33.568
We have heard the impassioned demands of the victors who claim to make us pay as if we were the vanquished.

00:33:34.088 --> 00:33:35.349
and punish us as guilty.

00:33:36.190 --> 00:33:37.911
But we are not solely responsible.

00:33:38.732 --> 00:33:43.516
The imperialism of European countries has shaped the international situation.

00:33:44.718 --> 00:33:46.179
But we are not the only ones to blame.

00:33:46.599 --> 00:33:50.242
The imperialism of European countries has poisoned the international situation.

00:33:50.523 --> 00:33:51.824
Any other observations?

00:33:53.786 --> 00:33:54.606
The meeting is adjourned.

00:33:56.188 --> 00:33:57.129
No negotiations.

00:33:57.529 --> 00:33:58.630
15 days to respond,

00:33:59.030 --> 00:33:59.851
See you in early June.

00:34:01.800 --> 00:34:02.120
Indeed,

00:34:02.121 --> 00:34:03.521
The Treaty of Versailles is very harsh.

00:34:03.661 --> 00:34:08.864
but it would have been difficult for public opinion to accept a treaty that was not.

00:34:09.744 --> 00:34:11.205
Germany had to pay.

00:34:11.826 --> 00:34:12.826
Once the conditions are known,

00:34:13.186 --> 00:34:13.667
in Berlin,

00:34:14.307 --> 00:34:15.027
It's outrage.

00:34:15.528 --> 00:34:18.729
The way in which the German delegation was treated is considered unacceptable.

00:34:19.230 --> 00:34:20.490
We feel betrayed by Wilson.

00:34:20.770 --> 00:34:23.152
who had promised a dignified and just peace.

00:34:24.052 --> 00:34:28.934
If he hadn't said "with me everything will be different" and the outcome ultimately wasn't different,

00:34:28.935 --> 00:34:39.920
He created such an illusion that he created a desire for revenge which was maintained by the German military who hid from their people that it was they who had requested the armistice and not the civilian power.

00:34:40.220 --> 00:34:48.164
But from the moment the allies impose peace conditions on a republic that the people have not been able to negotiate.

00:34:49.705 --> 00:34:49.985
Well,

00:34:51.107 --> 00:34:54.852
The German people feel betrayed by the Weimar Republic.

00:34:55.193 --> 00:34:55.774
For the Germans,

00:34:55.914 --> 00:34:56.635
And we understand them.

00:34:57.563 --> 00:34:58.724
The Treaty of Versailles is a diktat.

00:34:59.004 --> 00:35:04.267
It was precisely because the victors could not reach an agreement that all these preliminaries were so lengthy.

00:35:04.887 --> 00:35:05.367
too long,

00:35:05.828 --> 00:35:06.468
and that at one point,

00:35:06.648 --> 00:35:07.849
Public opinion was somewhat there,

00:35:07.850 --> 00:35:09.430
that it was necessary to put an end to it,

00:35:09.470 --> 00:35:10.810
that it was still necessary to sign this treaty,

00:35:11.151 --> 00:35:13.052
Well, we impose it on the vanquished.

00:35:13.152 --> 00:35:13.792
And at the same time,

00:35:13.912 --> 00:35:14.512
seen from the other side,

00:35:14.853 --> 00:35:16.033
This is the ultimate humiliation.

00:35:17.014 --> 00:35:18.415
Germany is traumatized.

00:35:18.835 --> 00:35:19.635
From his point of view,

00:35:20.055 --> 00:35:22.637
She did not lose the war and does not feel responsible.

00:35:23.177 --> 00:35:26.199
She is overwhelmed by its 400 clauses and takes time to respond.

00:35:27.247 --> 00:35:28.928
In June 1919,

00:35:28.929 --> 00:35:29.768
Wilson has had enough.

00:35:30.248 --> 00:35:31.409
He wants to return to the United States.

00:35:31.949 --> 00:35:33.790
Clemenceau threatens to break the armistice.

00:35:34.210 --> 00:35:36.051
Foch is already bringing out his staff maps.

00:35:37.732 --> 00:35:38.032
Finally,

00:35:38.492 --> 00:35:39.172
June 28th,

00:35:39.793 --> 00:35:40.613
The treaty is signed.

00:35:40.953 --> 00:35:41.574
in Versailles.

00:35:42.554 --> 00:35:43.014
Eventually,

00:35:43.374 --> 00:35:45.295
The three negotiators got what they wanted.

00:35:45.856 --> 00:35:47.396
Wilson imposed his League of Nations.

00:35:47.956 --> 00:35:50.818
Lloyd George obtains the fleet and part of the German colonies.

00:35:51.418 --> 00:35:53.199
and Clemenceau secured his borders.

00:35:54.095 --> 00:35:58.656
But what the Allies underestimated with the staging and content of the Treaty of Versailles,

00:35:59.177 --> 00:36:01.517
It is the profound psychological impact that it will have afterwards.

00:36:02.397 --> 00:36:04.098
Humiliation is not the goal.

00:36:05.378 --> 00:36:06.679
But humiliation will be the result.

00:36:07.839 --> 00:36:08.939
The humiliation is not intentional.

00:36:09.200 --> 00:36:14.021
The aim is to make Germany understand that it cannot,

00:36:14.421 --> 00:36:16.402
that she must not do it again.

00:36:16.962 --> 00:36:17.422
However,

00:36:17.902 --> 00:36:18.822
Was it a bad treaty?

00:36:19.743 --> 00:36:20.543
Versailles has frozen.

00:36:21.467 --> 00:36:29.432
The Treaty of Versailles in 1919 was a major dilemma from the outset.

00:36:30.392 --> 00:36:30.813
On one hand,

00:36:31.413 --> 00:36:33.854
There was the prospect of building a better world.

00:36:35.555 --> 00:36:35.856
And that,

00:36:36.576 --> 00:36:37.817
That was Wilson's wish.

00:36:39.878 --> 00:36:40.698
And on the other hand,

00:36:41.499 --> 00:36:47.002
There was the ambition of the British and the French to divide the world according to their own criteria.

00:36:49.127 --> 00:36:58.732
The trauma experienced by all European peoples is such that the peace treaty is probably not a good treaty.

00:36:59.432 --> 00:37:05.216
but that it was perhaps the least bad treaty that could be negotiated at that time,

00:37:05.816 --> 00:37:06.656
under those conditions.

00:37:06.816 --> 00:37:11.479
The treaty was no more unjust than any other treaty that had resulted in a victory.

00:37:12.339 --> 00:37:12.960
If the Germans,

00:37:12.961 --> 00:37:13.460
at the time,

00:37:13.820 --> 00:37:15.001
had not been so crazy,

00:37:15.481 --> 00:37:18.883
They should have understood that the Peace of Versailles was a reasonable peace.

00:37:19.424 --> 00:37:23.746
But I can only conclude that the war had truly driven them mad.

00:37:28.629 --> 00:37:30.230
Following the Treaty of Versailles,

00:37:30.670 --> 00:37:31.991
Four more treaties will follow.

00:37:32.472 --> 00:37:34.193
They are said to be from the Paris region.

00:37:35.693 --> 00:37:36.434
Saint-Germain-en-Laye,

00:37:36.694 --> 00:37:38.035
which determines the fate of Austria.

00:37:39.655 --> 00:37:41.496
The Trianon at Versailles for Hungary,

00:37:43.817 --> 00:37:47.740
Neuilly, where Bulgaria loses part of its territory and access to the sea,

00:37:48.840 --> 00:37:51.662
and Sèvres, which will decide the future of the Ottoman Empire.

00:37:54.663 --> 00:37:58.265
All these treaties profoundly changed the face of this old Europe of empires.

00:37:58.826 --> 00:38:01.928
States are gradually organizing themselves and peace is slowly making its way.

00:38:02.648 --> 00:38:03.608
For nearly ten years,

00:38:03.969 --> 00:38:06.330
Europe will become an extraordinary laboratory.

00:38:06.850 --> 00:38:07.951
The treaties are becoming more flexible.

00:38:08.235 --> 00:38:11.817
German industry is recovering, and the first Franco-German partnership in history,

00:38:12.157 --> 00:38:14.037
Aristide Briand and Gustav Stressmann,

00:38:14.378 --> 00:38:16.458
win the Nobel Peace Prize in 1926.

00:38:17.499 --> 00:38:17.999
In Germany,

00:38:18.319 --> 00:38:19.260
the Weimar Republic,

00:38:19.660 --> 00:38:20.780
thanks to American capital,

00:38:21.260 --> 00:38:22.001
regains confidence.

00:38:22.541 --> 00:38:24.022
Relations with the neighbors are easing.

00:38:24.442 --> 00:38:26.403
We almost forget Versailles and its dictates.

00:38:29.604 --> 00:38:31.485
It would be a mistake to think that it's the treaty,

00:38:31.985 --> 00:38:36.767
its humiliation and its clauses which nourished the breeding ground of German Nazism and Italian Fascism.

00:38:37.347 --> 00:38:42.272
and driving to the worst.

00:38:43.193 --> 00:38:48.518
I don't think we can accuse the Treaty of Versailles of planting the seeds that caused the Second World War to explode.

00:38:48.538 --> 00:38:52.361
In 1929,

00:38:52.642 --> 00:38:58.067
France and Germany were considering the establishment of a customs union and the idea of ​​creating the United States of Europe.

00:38:59.828 --> 00:39:00.269
In Europe,

00:39:00.629 --> 00:39:01.930
There was no threat of war.

00:39:05.027 --> 00:39:07.937
A far more devastating event sweeps away this somewhat dark legend.

00:39:11.131 --> 00:39:12.092
The financial crisis,

00:39:12.352 --> 00:39:14.353
then the American economic crisis of 1929.

00:39:14.653 --> 00:39:15.534
will plunge Europe back into crisis,

00:39:15.694 --> 00:39:16.534
still recovering,

00:39:16.755 --> 00:39:18.356
and more specifically Germany,

00:39:18.576 --> 00:39:19.096
in chaos.

00:39:20.017 --> 00:39:22.118
She is the one responsible for the war that threatens.

00:39:22.638 --> 00:39:24.019
She's the one who's going to create unemployment.

00:39:24.319 --> 00:39:25.860
misery and instilling fear.

00:39:26.701 --> 00:39:27.701
Fear of communism,

00:39:27.962 --> 00:39:28.482
on the other hand,

00:39:28.762 --> 00:39:29.563
of the insurrection.

00:39:30.243 --> 00:39:35.707
And to give rise to a radical ideology that will resurrect the resentment and revenge of a peace that cannot be accepted.

00:39:37.775 --> 00:39:38.316
In Italy,

00:39:38.796 --> 00:39:40.258
Mussolini used Versailles,

00:39:40.598 --> 00:39:42.440
But that is not the reason for the rise of fascism.

00:39:44.882 --> 00:39:49.327
Mussolini had said from the beginning that the Treaty of Versailles should be reviewed and modified.

00:39:49.347 --> 00:39:53.491
From 1921 onwards,

00:39:53.492 --> 00:39:57.495
There has been a backlash against the communist party which is planning a revolution.

00:39:57.675 --> 00:40:01.496
like the one Lenin did.

00:40:02.076 --> 00:40:04.857
Fascism was not supported by major industrialists.

00:40:05.117 --> 00:40:06.618
but by the smallest manufacturers,

00:40:07.098 --> 00:40:12.179
as he had been supported by the large landowners who had feared being expropriated by the Communist Party.

00:40:13.479 --> 00:40:20.822
That is why these small industrialists helped the rise of fascism by supporting a government that promised to enforce order.

00:40:21.562 --> 00:40:22.582
Fear of Bolshevism,

00:40:22.942 --> 00:40:24.242
an exacerbated desire for order,

00:40:24.523 --> 00:40:25.863
humiliation of a bad peace.

00:40:26.247 --> 00:40:30.089
The same mechanism was put in place a few years later with the rise of the Nazis.

00:40:33.170 --> 00:40:42.434
Hitler's initial success in those crisis years of the 1920s came at precisely the moment when people in Germany were beginning to take a massive interest in the First World War again.

00:40:44.915 --> 00:40:47.236
The Treaty of Versailles will once again take center stage.

00:40:47.436 --> 00:40:49.337
serving as a pretext for impeccable propaganda.

00:40:50.357 --> 00:40:54.779
Hitler promised from the beginning that he would repair the peace of shame.

00:40:56.427 --> 00:41:02.850
who will restore the honor of the soldiers and will go and reconquer the lost homeland.

00:41:03.530 --> 00:41:07.872
He wants to build monuments for the defeated soldiers.

00:41:08.552 --> 00:41:13.054
And the war wounded will receive all the honors they did not receive from the Weimar Republic.

00:41:14.455 --> 00:41:14.855
That was it.

00:41:14.915 --> 00:41:15.735
Hitler's promise.

00:41:16.956 --> 00:41:18.957
Of course Versailles has a connection with Hitler.

00:41:19.937 --> 00:41:22.758
Of course Versailles has a link with the Second World War.

00:41:25.059 --> 00:41:29.121
But Versailles was not the cause of the Second World War.

00:41:31.902 --> 00:41:32.762
Corporal Hitler,

00:41:32.802 --> 00:41:34.283
who only feels comfortable within the army,

00:41:34.603 --> 00:41:36.904
will make the Treaty of Versailles his personal obsession.

00:41:37.784 --> 00:41:38.364
In his madness,

00:41:38.825 --> 00:41:43.146
His goal is to end this war that the Germans interrupted on November 11, 1918.

00:41:43.647 --> 00:41:44.767
in undignified conditions.

00:41:46.028 --> 00:41:50.829
By systematically trampling on the treaty clauses regarding rearmament and the annexation of the Sudetenland and Austria,

00:41:51.170 --> 00:41:51.850
it triggers,

00:41:52.050 --> 00:41:52.830
on a pretext,

00:41:53.491 --> 00:41:54.451
World War II.

00:41:59.991 --> 00:42:02.072
